# O1 is S17's denial that "the unlearned" learn. S17 sets the unlearned against the clever boys who took in the dictation, so there it means the dull.
# C1 (S13) and A1 use the word for the ignorant, those who do not yet know what they are learning.
# The ignorant can acquire knowledge while the dull do not grasp the dictation, so O1 can be true while C1 is true. O1 only contradicts C1 through this shift.
# "learn" also moves, from acquiring knowledge (S11, S13) to understanding a dictation (S15–S17).
# No premise or assumption carries the shift. A2 stays in the clever/dull sense throughout, and the move happens only between C1 and O1. So I name no bridge.
